WEBVTT

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:07.490
This is the Eevee Evolution Laboratory.

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:11.740
Today, Koharu’s Eevee
is having a medical checkup.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.620
Everything is in order.
She’s the picture of health.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:17.330
That’s a relief.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:22.000
So, what have you and Eevee
been doing lately?

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.960
We went to meet a Nymphia!

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:29.470
I even entered a contest
as a Pokémon Perfomer with her...

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:32.260
...and she performed with Fairy Wind.

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:34.430
Fairy Wind, hmm...?

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:37.810
I’d have loved to see
your performance.

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:43.940
Then we went to meet
the Eevee of a friend in Alola, Suiren.

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.740
One more choice.
The Eevee path.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:48.570
Huh?

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:51.610
Staying an Eevee.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.330
Like Satoshi’s Pikachu.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:56.450
Satoshi’s Pikachu?

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:02.960
I get it!
So Eevee have nine paths, not just eight!

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:06.090
Suiren taught me something.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:08.380
Eevee has lots of possibilities!

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:11.380
Yes, yes, you have that right!

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.590
And so, you two have met...

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:19.140
Eevee, and... Showers,
Thunders, Booster, Eefee...

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:23.650
Blacky, Leafia, Glacia, Nymphia...

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:26.110
Each of her evolved forms.

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:27.190
Right!

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:30.150
And did she show interest
in any of them?

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:31.990
Of course!

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:34.530
Or well, how do I put it?

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:36.910
She loved all of them...

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:39.950
...and couldn’t seem to choose
between them.

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:41.370
I see...

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:51.880
Sis!

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.460
Dinner’s ready!

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:05.390
Dad... Why is it
that Pokémon evolve?

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:14.980
Humans evolve by growing older year after year
and growing up slowly little by little, right?

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:18.150
But Pokémon evolution
is completely different...

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:19.910
Don’t they just wanna
get stronger?

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:21.740
That could be the case.

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:25.660
Some Pokémon might evolve
to become stronger.

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:29.960
The more I think about evolution,

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:35.760
the less sure I am about whether
Eevee wants to evolve or just stay as she is...

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:37.050
Amazing!

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:37.550
Huh?

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:41.550
You really are having
great experiences alongside Eevee!

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:43.100
Don’t tease me.

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:44.930
Oh, sorry.

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:47.930
“Why exactly do Pokémon evolve?”...

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:53.400
That’s something even we Pokémon Professors
consider an age-old question.

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:55.150
Really?

00:04:55.690 --> 00:05:00.360
Taken to extremes, you could say there are
as many reasons to evolve as there are Pokémon.

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:02.620
As many as there are Pokémon?!

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:09.870
Each and every human being
is one of a kind.

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:13.420
A unique existence of their own.
It’s the same idea.

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:16.550
Now I’m even less sure...

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:20.170
Oh, I know!

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:23.300
Koharu! Why don’t we
go camping this weekend?

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:24.180
Huh?

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:25.890
Camping! Yay!

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:29.770
I’d love to go! It’s been a while since
we last went out for a relaxing nature walk.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:33.020
Come on, Big Sis, let’s go!

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:35.230
Sure!

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:39.280
We’re off.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:44.740
We’ll head there as soon as
soccer club’s over.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:50.080
No! Wanpachi,
you’re going with me!

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:53.670
Take care of them, Wanpachi.

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:55.130
Okay, we’ll see you later.

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:57.000
See you later!

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:19.400
Koharu? Are you awake?

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:20.740
Are we there?

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:21.530
No...

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:25.160
I wanted to drop by somewhere
on the way.

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:31.540
What a big forest!

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:37.130
Is this the place
you wanted to drop by?

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:38.250
Yeah.

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:44.470
Lots of Pokémon
live in this forest.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:47.220
Ah, Butterfree!

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:04.860
I bet Go would be really excited
if he saw this forest.

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:06.360
Satoshi, too.

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:11.620
When Go’s done with Project Mew and
Satoshi’s done with the Masters Tournament,

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:13.450
we’ve gotta bring them here!

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:16.210
Ooh, that’s a good idea!

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:17.960
Shh!

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:30.430
It’s so cute!

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:34.980
Nyoromo. Tadpole Pokémon.
Water type.

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:41.940
The spiral on its belly is its internal organs showing through,
and its direction is said to differ by area.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:44.610
It’s headed towards the pond.

00:07:58.420 --> 00:07:59.080
Eevee!

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:27.150
Oh, my...

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:30.910
Where did you come from?

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:32.410
Mr. Enoki!

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:35.120
Sakuragi!

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:36.950
I haven’t seen you in so long.

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:39.330
That’s my Eevee you have there.

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:42.750
Oh, I see, I see. Here.

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:47.800
Oh, Eevee...

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:56.770
It evolved!

00:08:58.020 --> 00:09:01.270
Nyorozo. Tadpole Pokémon.
Water type.

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:06.610
Capable of living in or out of water.
Its body surface is always wet and slick.

00:09:06.610 --> 00:09:10.150
Staring at the swirl on its belly
causes drowsiness.

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:14.370
Koharu, Mr. Enoki here
is this forest’s caretaker.

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:17.540
He took care of me a lot
when I was young.

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:19.160
When you were young?!

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:22.630
He still helps out
with my research, even now.

00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:26.000
Oh, I really don’t do much.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.630
Nice to meet you.

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:29.840
Nice to meet you, I’m Koharu.

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:33.720
Sakuragi Koharu, huh...?
That’s a nice name.

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:43.350
You’ve grown this
into a marvelous forest, Mr. Enoki.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:46.650
Thank you.
It’s taken this long to do it.

00:09:47.070 --> 00:09:49.690
Forests can grow?

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:55.410
Yes... This forest was made
by humans planting trees.

00:09:55.410 --> 00:10:01.160
Back when your father was a kid,
the trees hadn’t grown this tall...

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:05.290
...and there weren’t
so many different flowers.

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:08.090
Does that mean there
were less Pokémon, too?

00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:11.800
Sure does. Not anywhere <i>near</i>
as many as there are now.

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:17.470
Still... When I was young,
this place felt like an enchanted forest.

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:34.700
“Madatsubomi. Flower Pokémon.
Grass/Poison type.

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:37.370
“It prefers hot and
humid environments.

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:42.040
“It is quick at capturing prey
with its vines.”

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:43.870
...it says! It’s amazing!

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:45.710
“Amazing” is right!

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:48.290
And not <i>just</i> the Pokémon!

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:51.710
Me, you, the plants...
They’re all amazing!

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:53.260
I’m amazing too?

00:10:53.260 --> 00:10:54.760
Yeah!

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:57.340
Just being alive’s amazing,
all on its own!

00:10:57.340 --> 00:11:00.060
It is?!

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:03.560
So you went through
experiences like that, too!

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:06.770
That was back when I was
about as small as Sota is now.

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:11.110
And now,
that boy is a Pokémon Professor.

00:11:11.110 --> 00:11:13.860
How time flies...

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:15.200
Oh!

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:19.330
That reminds me, Sakuragi,
one time you rescued a Pippi, right?

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:22.330
Huh? Tell me about that!

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:26.370
I remember that day well.

00:11:34.550 --> 00:11:36.300
Pocket Monsters!

00:11:58.030 --> 00:11:59.990
Stop!

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:05.120
Stop, stop, stop, stop, stop!

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:08.370
Don’t bully it!

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:21.930
“Pippi. Fairy Pokémon.
Fairy type.

00:12:21.930 --> 00:12:24.260
“Its behavior and appearance
are adorable.

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:31.770
“It is said that happiness will come to those who
see a gathering of Pippi dancing under a full moon.”

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:36.570
Pippi are supposed to live
deeper in the mountains...

00:12:36.570 --> 00:12:39.490
This one might be lost.

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:41.780
Are you lost?

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:44.950
It’ll be okay. There, there...

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:49.040
After that,

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:52.790
I came here every day
so I could visit Pippi.

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:55.050
Here!

00:12:58.010 --> 00:13:00.550
Then, once Pippi could walk again,

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:03.550
we walked around
the forest together.

00:13:03.930 --> 00:13:06.390
Look! Those are cherry blossoms!

00:13:03.930 --> 00:13:06.390
sakura

00:13:06.390 --> 00:13:08.560
Aren’t they pretty?

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:11.190
Their name is just like mine.

00:13:12.690 --> 00:13:15.820
That’s why I love cherry blossoms!

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:24.450
That’s Pippi’s
Finger Wiggle move.

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:27.540
You never know what move
will come out—

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:31.080
So I was going to say,
be careful...

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:35.590
I-I-I-I’m a-a-a-all r-r-r-right...

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:41.340
The days I spent with Pippi
were so much fun.

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:44.390
But, in the end...

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:48.350
It was time to say goodbye.

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:49.560
Pippi...

00:13:54.150 --> 00:13:56.190
Pippi!

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:17.130
That’s Petal Blizzard!

00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:19.380
Cherry blossom petals!

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:26.140
Thank you, Pippi!

00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:36.730
It must have been saying thanks.

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:39.270
Giving you its thanks.

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:44.860
I wonder how
that Pippi’s doing now...

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:47.490
Who knows...?
But I hope it’s doing well.

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:49.540
It has to be!

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:51.120
I think you’re right.

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:57.250
Now, then...
We should head to the campsite.

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:05.430
Sorry, sorry!

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:09.600
<i>Delicious!</i>

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:16.600
How pretty!

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:19.610
The moon’s full and round.

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:23.860
Eevee?

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:24.860
Wanpachi?

00:15:25.240 --> 00:15:26.700
What could it be?

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:27.410
Shh!

00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:30.740
I can hear it...

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:32.240
Hear what?

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:38.000
We might be incredibly
lucky tonight!

00:15:46.930 --> 00:15:48.050
Those voices...

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:49.470
Pippi?

00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:50.430
Yeah.

00:15:50.430 --> 00:15:52.390
Tonight’s a full moon,

00:15:52.390 --> 00:15:55.060
so I thought there was a chance...

00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:04.400
Sometimes, Pippi gather and dance
under the full moon,

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:06.700
holding an evolution ritual.

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:09.200
Using Moon Stones!

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:14.450
There’s an old legend that says
happiness comes to those who see Pippi dance.

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:18.120
This is a very important
ritual for them.

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:20.330
Let’s watch,
but no disturbing them!

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:23.670
Come along, now.

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:49.780
There’s a Pixie, too...

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:50.700
Huh?

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:01.330
Oh, no!

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:02.330
Golbat!

00:17:02.710 --> 00:17:05.130
In the middle of their ritual...

00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:06.840
How could they?!

00:17:14.390 --> 00:17:15.260
They’re coming back!

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:17.180
Eevee!

00:17:29.740 --> 00:17:31.240
Eevee...

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:33.870
Got it.

00:17:33.870 --> 00:17:35.990
Eevee, use Psychokinesis!

00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:56.140
Look! The Pippi!

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:19.830
Thank you for showing us the ritual!

00:18:44.230 --> 00:18:46.480
Huh?! R-Right...

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:09.630
Dad! Could that Pixie have been...?

00:19:11.090 --> 00:19:12.130
Yeah!

00:19:23.060 --> 00:19:25.100
Can’t sleep?

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:26.810
No...

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:31.480
Sorry, sorry.
Did I wake you up?

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:35.990
Those evolving Pippi
were so beautiful.

00:19:35.990 --> 00:19:39.990
Beautiful, mysterious,
and warm, too...

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:43.750
I... think I understand it a bit now.

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:48.500
What you said about there being
as many kinds of evolution as there are Pokémon,

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:52.300
and each and every one
being unique.

00:19:52.300 --> 00:19:53.510
You do?

00:19:53.510 --> 00:19:56.510
Were you happy
to see that Pippi again?

00:19:56.510 --> 00:19:58.840
Happy doesn’t begin to cover it!

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:02.140
Experiencing a miracle like that,
it really makes me want to...

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:08.560
...make a world where people and Pokémon
can cuddle up close and live happily together, forever!

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:12.400
Which is why I have to
keep up my research!

00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:14.150
It reaffirms that conviction of mine.

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:15.940
Huh?

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:19.530
There’s something cool
about you today, Dad!

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:21.030
R-Really?

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:23.290
You’re nothing like
your usual self.

00:20:23.290 --> 00:20:25.160
I-I see...

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:29.120
Oh, well...
As long as I’m cool for today...

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:31.420
Dad!

00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:32.170
Huh?

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:36.050
I want to learn more about
Pokémon evolution!

00:20:37.470 --> 00:20:40.390
Not just because of Eevee...

00:20:40.390 --> 00:20:42.050
Though that’s part of it...

00:20:42.430 --> 00:20:46.060
Right now,
I just want to learn a lot more about it!

00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:49.730
Then, you can just start by walking.

00:20:49.730 --> 00:20:51.440
Together with Eevee.

00:20:51.860 --> 00:20:55.860
Of course, there may still be
many paths for you to choose from.

00:20:56.490 --> 00:21:00.450
If you reach a crossroad,
just listen to your own feelings.

00:21:00.450 --> 00:21:04.080
Listen to them
and choose your next path.

00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:07.000
After all, your possibilities are...

00:21:07.750 --> 00:21:08.960
Plenty?

00:21:09.290 --> 00:21:11.420
Plenty doesn’t cut it!

00:21:12.130 --> 00:21:13.460
They’re endless!

00:21:15.090 --> 00:21:18.550
Our possibilities are... endless!

00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:26.180
Eevee...
Let’s always be there for each other!

00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:33.770
Today, and its events, have etched themselves
deep inside Koharu’s heart.

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:37.860
With their steps ever so slightly
firmer than before,

00:21:37.860 --> 00:21:43.280
Koharu and Eevee will keep moving
ever forward.

00:23:06.160 --> 00:23:10.120
Breaking news!
Pokémon World Championships News!

00:23:06.160 --> 00:23:08.830
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:23:08.830 --> 00:23:15.500
I’ve got my plans for when I grow up in my pocket

00:23:11.160 --> 00:23:15.500
The Masters Tournament,
the fest to crown the world’s strongest, has begun!

00:23:16.080 --> 00:23:19.960
Cameras dive behind the scenes
of these fierce fights!

00:23:16.750 --> 00:23:21.710
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:23:21.170 --> 00:23:26.930
Catch the secrets behind the competitors’ might
and find out what to keep your eyes on, only on our show!

00:23:21.710 --> 00:23:26.010
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:23:26.010 --> 00:23:27.300
Let’s have a fight!

00:23:27.300 --> 00:23:29.930
1. Once the battle’s done

00:23:27.970 --> 00:23:32.100
Will we find out the secret of how dark horse
Competitor Satoshi sped through the ranks?!

00:23:29.930 --> 00:23:32.100
2. And we’re laughing or crying

00:23:32.100 --> 00:23:35.440
Don’t miss the next episode!

00:23:32.100 --> 00:23:35.440
On 3, let’s be...
